data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign report: greet, tested\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## Outcome: met\\n\\n## What happened\\n- Dispatched the full task to `dev` (dispatch d002) in a single round.\\n- `dev` implemented `src/greet.py` (`greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`)\\n  and `tests/test_greet.py` (tests `test_normal_name` and `test_empty_string`),\\n  committed as `f529927e2666a6a73c2a6feac7b4512ba965df5d` on branch\\n  `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`.\\n- Verified independently (not just trusting dev's report): fetched dev's\\n  branch into the orchestrator's local subject clone, checked out commit\\n  `f529927` in a throwaway worktree, and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself from that tree.\\n  Result: `Ran 2 tests in 0.000s / OK`, exit code 0.\\n- Confirmed file contents directly via `git show` against the committed\\n  commit (not dev's working tree) to rule out an uncommitted/stale report.\\n- Accepted dev's d002 on this evidence.\\n\\n## Verdict\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied and independently confirmed:\\n1. `src/greet.py` exists with correct `greet(name)` behavior.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name and the empty string.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0.\\n\\nNo rework was needed; this closed in one dispatch round.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

